From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:14:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] resolve stylo OpaqueNodes through the slot index

BlitzNode::opaque packs the NodeId into stylo's usize OpaqueNode. On
wasm32 that keeps only the slot index and drops the version, so
NodeId::from_u64(opaque) rebuilt the key at version 1 and missed every
node in a reused slot. The animation sweep read the miss as "not in
the document" and cleared the node's transitions and animations on
each resolve, so they never advanced. The snapshot cleanup and the
:has() invalidation walk skipped those nodes the same way.

example.com rebuilds each paragraph with innerHTML. The first span of
every paragraph after the first lands in the slot the previous parse's
fragment root freed, and its opacity transition never ran.

NodeTree now keeps each slot index's current id, and id_from_opaque
resolves through it on any pointer width.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: NodeTree is a struct with named fields
now, so the slot index map is the slot_ids field.
---
 src/document.rs |  5 ++---
 src/stylo.rs    | 18 ++++++++----------
 src/tree.rs     | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index eedc2ad..f1e7e21 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -1910,9 +1910,8 @@ impl BaseDocument {
     // triggered it queued, and every retry re-panics (livelock).
     pub fn clear_style_snapshots(&mut self) {
         for opaque in self.snapshots.keys() {
-            let id = NodeId::from_u64(opaque.id() as u64);
-            if let Some(node) = self.nodes.get_mut(id) {
-                node.set_has_snapshot(false);
+            if let Some(id) = self.nodes.id_from_opaque(opaque.id()) {
+                self.nodes[id].set_has_snapshot(false);
             }
         }
         self.snapshots.clear();
